<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

    <PropertyGroup>
        <TargetFramework>net11.0</TargetFramework>
        <LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>
        <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
        <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
        <IsPackable>true</IsPackable>
        <PackageId>JRK.JevRunner.Image</PackageId>
        <Title>JRK JevRunner Image</Title>
        <Authors>Jeppe Roi Kristensen</Authors>
        <Description>Optional SkiaSharp image helpers for JRK.JevRunner. Validate image files, proportionally upscale or downscale them, and render normalized Jev bounding-box answers without modifying source files.</Description>
        <PackageTags>jev;typesafe;ai;system-one;images;bounding-box;skiasharp;dotnet</PackageTags>
        <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/jeppevammenkristensen/all</PackageProjectUrl>
        <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/jeppevammenkristensen/all</RepositoryUrl>
        <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
        <PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
        <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
        <PackageIcon>Runner-Icon.png</PackageIcon>
        <PackageReleaseNotes>Initial release: optional SkiaSharp image helpers for JRK.JevRunner.

Image scaling
- ImageScaler.Upscale and Downscale scale proportionally using the shorter and longer side, respectively, with custom bounds (280 and 1568 by default).
- Scaling returns PNG bytes without modifying the source. Results still outside other API limits are not rejected.

Image validation
- ImageValidator inspects actual PNG/JPEG contents and checks inclusive 280-1568-pixel width and height and the 16 MiB file limit.
- Rejects animated PNG and non-default EXIF orientation. Checks pixel decoding when other checks pass.
- ImageValidationResult exposes typed dimension or string errors, SuggestedScaling, and ThrowIfInvalid(). Errors provide GetErrorMessage(); ImageDimensionError.GetErrors() checks custom dimension bounds.
- SuggestedScaling groups dimension violations by direction. It ignores other errors and does not guarantee valid resized output.

Experimental automatic adjustment
- AddImageAssetWithAutoAdjustment validates, attempts one suggested resize, and registers the result without changing source files.
- Unchanged files retain their detected format and bytes; resized images become PNG.
- Validation, byte loading, and resizing consistently use the supplied file system.
- Adjusted output is not revalidated. Request-wide limits require separate validation.

Bounding-box rendering
- BoxRenderer.DrawBox accepts a single BoxAnswer or an enumerable through the AppliedBox union.
- Draws normalized bounding-box outlines with shared configurable color and stroke width.

Platform and file-system support
- Renderer, validator, and scaler support injectable file access through TruePath and IFileSystem.
- Includes Linux native assets alongside SkiaSharp's Windows and macOS assets.
- Targets .NET 11 and uses preview C# union support.</PackageReleaseNotes>
        <LangVersion>preview</LangVersion>
    </PropertyGroup>

    <ItemGroup>
      <None Update="README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
      <None Include="..\LICENSE" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
      <None Include="..\JRK.JevRunner\assets\Runner-Icon.png" Pack="true" PackagePath="Runner-Icon.png" />
    </ItemGroup>

    <ItemGroup>
      <PackageReference Include="SkiaSharp" Version="4.153.1" />
      <PackageReference Include="SkiaSharp.NativeAssets.Linux.NoDependencies" Version="4.153.1" />
      <ProjectReference Include="..\JRK.JevRunner\JRK.JevRunner.csproj" />
    </ItemGroup>

</Project>
